{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/857994-kith-and-appearance","id":857994,"title":"Kith and Appearance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-02T16:27:25-07:00","id":857994,"title":"Kith and Appearance","content":"Ideas on how to explain a Nocker, Redcap, Boggan, or just about any kind of thallain with a high APP? just think its worth asking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T05:57:06-07:00","id":858298,"title":"","content":"Well, seelie Redcaps are very handsome in book. Unseelie ones could be charismatic though. I think nockers can hav high appearance points. And others, if you don't like stereotypes why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T09:59:50-07:00","id":858384,"title":"","content":"Yes im sure they could exist but asking what they'd look like...<br /> <br /> A high appearance boggan, should have a good natured and fair face maybe being a litttle less plump then other boggans...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:15:57-07:00","id":858713,"title":"","content":"I don't have my books handy, but - in general - changelings look thematically appropriate. So take the underlying idea, and try to picture a version that others would find attractive. Changelings are creatures of human fantasies - play to the tropes. <br /> <br /> Nockers, for example, come from myths of dwarves and supernatural metalworkers. So a handsome male nocker probably has a &quot;hunky handyman&quot;-vibe to him. Big and strong, with rippling muscles and six-pack abs - maybe a rugged looking beard. When he takes off his shirt, all hot and sweaty from his latest project, every girl in the area stops to watch as he pours a bucket of cool water over his head. Even the jaded girl who just got her heart broken finds that she loses her train of thought for a moment . . .<br /> <br /> With a redcap, he's the bad-boy-your-mama-warned-you-to-stay-away-from. He's got the piercings, the tattoos, the bike . . . He's the bad influence that makes you want to walk on the wild side. <br /> <br /> For the boggan? What girl doesn't like a guy who can cook? He always smells like something yummy. He probably made (or at least altered) his clothes, so they look perfect on him . . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:09:32-07:00","id":858751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/857994-kith-and-appearance#post857994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas on how to explain a Nocker, Redcap, Boggan, or just about any kind of thallain with a high APP? just think its worth asking...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well changelings have both a fae mien and a human form. They might be gorgeous (by human standards) in their mortal seeming and repulsive (by those same standards) in their fae mien. But it's also worth noting that most redcaps don't necessarily see each other as repulsive. Indeed, even most other fae are used to them, and their ideals of beauty might be quite different to our own.<br /> <br /> Take for example human cultures. What's considered beautiful in, say, West Africa, might be completely different to what's considered beautiful in Western Europe. Beauty is in the eye of the beholder and attractiveness is, to a degree, a cultural thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T19:29:47-07:00","id":863438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/857994-kith-and-appearance?p=858384#post858384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes im sure they could exist but asking what they'd look like...<br /> <br /> A high appearance boggan, should have a good natured and fair face maybe being a litttle less plump then other boggans...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like to point out that being plump/round/curvy doesn't mean you can't have a high Appearance, and a high Appearance doesn't mean you're thinner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:45:22-07:00","id":863720,"title":"","content":"Appearance has always been a tough stat this way. It's quite subjective and awkward to put on a graduated scale of measured increments. I think this is one of the reasons they did away with it as an attribute in NWoD/ChroD, opting instead to make it a merit. I wouldn't worry about the description of a high Appearance, just the fact that they have it. Does your description of them correspond with what you think Appearance 3 should be? If they have Appearance 3 the answer is yes, if the answer is no than however you described them corresponds with whatever Appearance they have, whether it be 1 or 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:32:25-07:00","id":864076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/857994-kith-and-appearance?p=863720#post863720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appearance has always been a tough stat this way. It's quite subjective and awkward to put on a graduated scale of measured increments. I think this is one of the reasons they did away with it as an attribute in NWoD/ChroD, opting instead to make it a merit. I wouldn't worry about the description of a high Appearance, just the fact that they have it. Does your description of them correspond with what you think Appearance 3 should be? If they have Appearance 3 the answer is yes, if the answer is no than however you described them corresponds with whatever Appearance they have, whether it be 1 or 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Later developments that kept it (Adventure! and EX3) eventually made it a memorable and inspiring feature, with being hot/horrifying as a toggle extra. You chose whether your inspiring air came from good looks or bad ones, and any swing from the norm was a large number of dots either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:38:26-07:00","id":864078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/857994-kith-and-appearance?p=858751#post858751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take for example human cultures. What's considered beautiful in, say, West Africa, might be completely different to what's considered beautiful in Western Europe. Beauty is in the eye of the beholder and attractiveness is, to a degree, a cultural thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent it is, but we can overemphasize cultural aspects of beauty. &quot;Attractive&quot; is nature's way of demonstrating the person is good and healthy and able to produce children. Appropriate body ratios, symmetrical features, those physical features which suggest a healthy supply of the right hormones - they appear as attractive across all cultures. There are always variations and people do have personal preferences, but there is something universal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T02:47:43-07:00","id":864187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/857994-kith-and-appearance?p=864078#post864078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To an extent it is, but we can overemphasize cultural aspects of beauty. &quot;Attractive&quot; is nature's way of demonstrating the person is good and healthy and able to produce children. Appropriate body ratios, symmetrical features, those physical features which suggest a healthy supply of the right hormones - they appear as attractive across all cultures. There are always variations and people do have personal preferences, but there is something universal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but some people don't find symmetry attractive either. People aren't machines and so they're not entirely hardwired by genetics and instinct. Some traits might be more generally appealing across the board, but culture and personal experience play a huge part too.<br /> <br /> My point was that beauty is in the eye of the beholder, and the fae part of the soul is otherworldly even if it's fused to a human soul. So an asymmetrical redcap may appear very appealing indeed to other redcaps.<br /> <br /> To be honest, Appearance is one of those traits you can't look at with too much of a critical eye, or it starts to collapse in on itself. In actuality, it overlaps quite a lot with what Charisma already does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T07:42:20-07:00","id":864285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/857994-kith-and-appearance?p=864187#post864187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but some people don't find symmetry attractive either. People aren't machines and so they're not entirely hardwired by genetics and instinct. Some traits might be more generally appealing across the board, but culture and personal experience play a huge part too.<br /> <br /> My point was that beauty is in the eye of the beholder, and the fae part of the soul is otherworldly even if it's fused to a human soul. So an asymmetrical redcap may appear very appealing indeed to other redcaps.<br /> <br /> To be honest, Appearance is one of those traits you can't look at with too much of a critical eye, or it starts to collapse in on itself. In actuality, it overlaps quite a lot with what Charisma already does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attributes are based on a view of qualities as separate from each other, when they are often related, and so will tend to come up short if you think about them for too long. Also, very ill-defined; Scientists studying animal behavior can't all agree on what intelligence is, so they don't use it as a technical term, referring instead to several divisions of cognition with particular definitions in the field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}